Mary here with a gamespot news update it  looks like Legend of Zelda for Wii U is  going to have a world as big as the  system hardware will allow longtime  Zelda series producer Eiji Aonuma said  in an interview with game reactor  magazine ever since we made the very  first generation of Legend of Zelda  we've had as large a world as can be  realized with the hardware so you could  say it was inevitable that we've now  done the same with the new wii u title  we've only caught a couple peaks at the  upcoming zelda and the scale definitely  seems much larger than anything we've  seen from the previous entries in the  series Shigeru Miyamoto said that the  Twilight Princess entire map would only  represent one area of the new game given  the size of the world the wii u zelda  game is frequently being referred to as  an open-world game onuma however takes  issue with that description not because  it's inaccurate but because zelda games  have always allowed you to roam and  explore a huge world the distinguishing  factor of the upcoming zelda according  to a NUMA is this time around the world  is a seamless one instead of being  segmented into several areas the new  zelda game is expected to come out  sometime this year so we'll likely have  more updates around it probably around  III so be sure to check out gamespot com  flash news for the latest
 

